==German==

===Etymology===
Originally called {{etyl|en|de}} ''[[cake]]s'' by Hermann Bahlsen, who brought the idea to Germany in 1889. From 1911 his company changed the name of the article to ''Keks''; at the time, the plural was also ''Keks''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/keːks/|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|g2=n|Kekses|Kekse}}

# [[cookie]] {{qualifier|US}}, [[biscuit]] {{qualifier|UK}}

====Usage notes====
The word is always masculine in northern and central Germany. In the southern half of the language area, it is often neuter.

====Related terms====
* [[Keksdose]]
* [[auf den Keks gehen]]

